# Never branch off Linear

Do not create a git branch unless it is `feature/RIDGE-n` for an issue that **already exists** on Linear.

A tangent, UX follow-up, or “while we are here” change stays on the current Linear branch. If that cannot work, **ask** before you create anything.

## Do not

- Name a branch after the work (`feature/add-tenant-on-unit`, `feature/fix-empty-picker`, or any name that is not `feature/RIDGE-n`)
- Create a Linear issue after the fact to justify a branch you already made
- Create a Linear issue so you can branch, unless this message asked you to create that issue

## Ask first, then wait

Stay on this ticket’s branch, or create a Linear issue first and then `feature/RIDGE-n`. Do not pick for them.
